    "description": "Transportation Equipment Network leases and services dry vans, refrigerated trailers, flatbeds, chassis-related equipment, and related fleet assets for transportation and logistics customers. Its customer base includes carriers, shippers, and logistics operators that need equipment availability, maintenance support, and fleet flexibility, and the business runs as an asset-heavy leasing platform with repair, technology, and fleet services. Public materials describe TEN as North America's second-largest full-service trailer lessor with a fleet of more than 83,000 trailers and locations across major logistics hubs in the United States and Canada. The current platform was created through the rebranding of Star Leasing and the 2024 combination with TIP Canada. I Squared Capital announced in July 2024 that QIA, Mubadala, and other co-investors had invested more than $600 million into TEN. The reviewed public materials do not disclose the detailed current ownership percentages for each shareholder.",
