    "description": "Transportation Equipment Network (TEN) is an asset-owning North American commercial-trailer leasing and fleet-services platform serving carriers, shippers and logistics operators. It provides trailer leasing and rentals, maintenance, fleet technology and advisory services, refrigerated-equipment support and storage through an integrated network assembled from Star Leasing, Cooling Concepts, NETS, Commercial Trailer Leasing, TIP Canada and Boston Trailer. Current company disclosures describe approximately 83,000 trailers, about 1,000 employees and nearly 50 locations across the United States and Canada. I Squared began building the platform through ISQ Global Infrastructure Fund II's March 2021 acquisition of employee-owned Star Leasing. TEN became the common trade identity effective July 1, 2024, when Mubadala, QIA and other co-investors invested more than $600 million. Meketa Infrastructure Fund and a separate ISQ Open Infrastructure Company Series II position are also publicly disclosed current interests. Exact post-2024 ownership percentages, securities and vehicles are not fully public; the only precise current percentage found is Series II's 6.29% indirect common-stock interest at March 31, 2026. No later platform sale or signed pending exit was identified through August 19, 2026.",
